# Copyable close on every note

Cursor shows a copy control on fenced code blocks, not on ordinary prose. There is no separate copy-icon API.

**Always** end every assistant note with a fenced code block as the last copyable content, so a copy control appears at the bottom of the note.

Do this on every reply, including short acknowledgements, STOP holds, and questions. Do not leave a note that ends only in prose.

Put the primary copyable fence last among copyable blocks. Brief context may go above. Do not put explanation, options, or follow-up questions after that fence, except the required CalibraytAI `END — <title>` line below.

What belongs in the closing fence:

- If Joel may need to paste something (Cursor prompt, `prompt?` reply, email, command, path, HEAD SHA, Alembic revision, report field block): that exact content.
- Otherwise: a compact copyable close of the note (key takeaway and next action).

Do this even when the same facts also appear in prose. Do not leave copyable commands or prompt text in prose only.

**CalibraytAI chat-title continuity:** After that primary fence, the only permitted trailing line is:

`END — <exact active ChatGPT development chat title>`

Do not put explanation, options, or follow-up questions after that END line. Canonical: `docs/governance/continuity-and-anti-drift.md`.

Keep secrets, passwords, and SECRET_KEY values out of chat, fenced or not.
